        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Nightingale's Song\n- People: Robert Timberg, John McCain, Bud McFarlane, Oliver North, John Poindexter, Jim Webb\n- Organizations: United States Naval Academy, United States Navy, United States Marine Corps, Baltimore Sun\n- Roles: journalist, political commentator, television host, military historian, author, Lieutenant Colonel\n- Topics: Vietnam War\n\nFacts:\n- Oliver North was born on October 7, 1943.\n- Oliver North is an American political commentator, television host, military historian, New York Times best-selling author, and former United States Marine Corps Lieutenant Colonel.\n- The Nightingale's Song is a 1995 book by Baltimore Sun journalist Robert Timberg.\n- The Nightingale's Song relates the military and political careers of five United States Naval Academy graduates: John McCain, Bud McFarlane, Oliver North, John Poindexter, and Jim Webb.\n- Most of the five United States Naval Academy graduates in The Nightingale's Song served during the Vietnam War in either the United States Navy or the United States Marine Corps.",
